{"kind":"assert","text":"Three decisions from Hugh at 10:31 EST, and the rulings that follow.\nStart the combined gate now.\n\nHugh's words, complete:\n\n\u003e gate-speed proposals: yes to 1, 2, 4.  Power supply should not be\n\u003e a factor in any of these decisions.\n\u003e Yes, builder can push.\n\n## 1. The push\n\nI asked Hugh this: \"Authorize the push of\n`builder/ctl1-promise-assertions-20261114`. The combined head\ncarries CTL-1, and its review request needs a pushed head.\" He\nanswered \"Yes, builder can push.\" The hold of 550d5ede ends. Push\nwith hooks on, as 550d5ede states.\n\n## 2. Power\n\nPower is no condition of a gate or of any run. I retire f27885cc,\n2adebce3, 4ff07ca6, 59a8080e and the note 48c64785. A run needs no\npower reading, no charge floor, no power sample and no sleep record.\nWhen a gate fails on a timeout, report it as any failure.\n\n## 3. The record of a gate (proposal 1)\n\nFrom now, a gate leaves this record and no more:\n\n1. A START act with the head, the tree and main.\n2. `npm run gate` once, in the lane's worktree at a clean head. Its\n   output goes to one log file in a new directory,\n   `~/play/artroom-evidence/\u003cdate\u003e-\u003chead-slug\u003e/`.\n3. An END act with the exit code, the wall time, the count lines of\n   each stage, and the SHA-256 of the log.\n4. The note's evidence table cites the log by path and SHA-256.\n\nThe gate prints the head, the tree and the count of changed files in\nits first lines, so the log names what it tested.\n\nThese go: the supervisor and its frozen plan, the hash lists of\nsource and tools, the root review of a plan, the copy of temporary\nand cache trees, the `SHA256SUMS` file, the read-only seal, the\nmanifest under `notes/implementation/evidence/`, the sleep\nsupplement, and the sealed record of a landing.\n\nThe formal focused interval goes too. A lane runs its changed test\nfiles and its controls as development checks under 07cd5911. Keep\nthe output of each control in the evidence directory, and cite it in\nthe note. `scripts/focused-check.mjs` stays in the tree as a tool.\n\nRecords that exist stand. The combined focused pass d5e93126 stands.\n\nThis rule is in force for each head filed after this act. The\ndocuments follow in request GS-1, which I file next.\n\n## 4. The queue\n\n1. Combined head 256673de: run `npm run gate` now, without the\n   supervisor of ded16024. Then push, file the review request.\n2. GS-1: the head that makes each later gate shorter.\n3. NF-5, C2, C3, then RV-1, CB-1, AE-1, P1.\n\nNF-5 owes its controls, its browser acceptance and one gate. It owes\nno formal focused run.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}